KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16 gcc16
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ saturated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
libstdc++ 16's saturating_add and saturating_cast (<numeric>, C++26).  With
GCC 16 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) only the WRONG assertion fails.  CBMC
failed to parse GCC 16's <utility> in C++26 mode (a pack expansion in a
subscript, cpp23_subscript_pack_expansion_forms), which <numeric> includes.
Tagged libstdcxx16: runs only where the host gcc is 16 or later.
